                                        "entry_id": "b8753d73-da36-36a6-85c0-3f4b1a5a21d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To position one’s belly; to move on one’s belly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5372fcac-ead8-4589-9e8e-0dda88873efa",
                                                "sense_id": "c6208e4e-d7c2-309f-a277-8e9874ecf6ee",
                                                "text": "Bellying forward to the edge of the clearing, he found Hans, lying on his face, feathered with arrows like a porcupine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                        "entry_id": "b8753d73-da36-36a6-85c0-3f4b1a5a21d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To swell and become protuberant; to bulge or billow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c7d80c2-5763-4894-bb95-c25c3f420684",
                                                "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                                "text": "The Pow'r appeaſ'd, with Winds ſuffic'd the Sail, / The bellying Canvaſs ſtrutted with the Gale; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ea41451-e3bb-492d-bc10-eb3d257fbdb9",
                                                "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                                "text": "The halliards twanged against the tops, the bunting bellied broad,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff2a202a-0ca1-4fd0-8ff5-45040f86d4d3",
                                                "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                                "text": "There were trees whose trunks bellied into huge swellings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42aa64f8-36e1-4fc5-85bf-30910c691997",
                                                "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                                "text": "1917 rev. 1925 Ezra Pound, \"Canto I\"\nwinds from sternward\nBore us onward with bellying canvas ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3758d6c4-1f9e-464a-8b3e-6fa592634c22",
                                                "sense_id": "4e441564-1bc0-36f7-974b-d3d6c1bda061",
                                                "text": "1930, Otis Adelbert Kline, The Prince of Peril, serialized in Argosy, Chapter 1,\nThe building stood on a circular foundation, and its walls, instead of mounting skyward in a straight line, bellied outward and then curved in again at the top."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0df794bc-a619-3775-a5a2-aca7994bbd4e",
                                        "entry_id": "b8753d73-da36-36a6-85c0-3f4b1a5a21d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to swell out; to fill."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29008d62-ed56-411f-936d-cae82b86f6df",
                                                "sense_id": "0df794bc-a619-3775-a5a2-aca7994bbd4e",
                                                "text": "A breeze which had crossed a thousand miles of wheat-lands bellied her taffeta skirt in a line so graceful, so full of animation and moving beauty, that the heart of a chance watcher on the lower road tightened to wistfulness over her quality of suspended freedom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1592823-5e58-47a5-95d3-ee8bd1e45ba8",
                                                "sense_id": "0df794bc-a619-3775-a5a2-aca7994bbd4e",
                                                "text": "Your breath of full consent bellied his sails; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
